{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PRO",
  "chapter": 21,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.21.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The king's heart ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the hand of the LORD, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the rivers of water: he turneth it whithersoever he will.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.21.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Every way of a man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " right in his own eyes: but the LORD pondereth the hearts.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.21.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To do justice and judgment ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " more acceptable to the LORD than sacrifice.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.21.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A high look, and a proud heart, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the plowing of the wicked, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " sin.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.21.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The thoughts of the diligent ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "tend",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " only to plenteousness; but of every one ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hasty only to want.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.21.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The getting of treasures by a lying tongue ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a vanity tossed to and fro by them that seek death.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.21.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The robbery of the wicked shall destroy them; because they refuse to do judgment.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.21.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The way of man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " froward and strange: but ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the pure, his work ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " right.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.21.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " better to dwell in a corner of the house-top, than with a brawling woman in a wide house.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.21.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The soul of the wicked desireth evil: his neighbor findeth no favor in his eyes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.21.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When the scorner is punished, the simple is made wise: and when the wise is instructed, he receiveth knowledge.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.21.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The righteous ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wisely considereth the house of the wicked: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "but God",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " overthroweth the wicked for ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wickedness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.21.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whoever stoppeth his ears at the cry of the poor, he also shall cry himself, but shall not be heard.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.21.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A gift in secret pacifieth anger: and a reward in the bosom, strong wrath.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.21.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " joy to the just to do judgment: but destruction ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to the workers of iniquity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.21.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The man that wandereth out of the way of understanding shall remain in the congregation of the dead.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.21.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that loveth pleasure ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a poor man: he that loveth wine and oil shall not be rich.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.21.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The wicked ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a ransom for the righteous, and the transgressor for the upright.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.21.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " better to dwell in the wilderness, than with a contentious and an angry woman.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.21.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a treasure to be desired, and oil in the dwelling of the wise; but a foolish man spendeth it up.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.21.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that followeth after righteousness and mercy findeth life, righteousness, and honor.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.21.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A wise ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " scaleth the city of the mighty, and casteth down the strength of its confidence.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.21.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whoever keepeth his mouth and his tongue keepeth his soul from troubles.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.21.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Proud ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " haughty scorner ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his name, who dealeth in proud wrath.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.21.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The desire of the slothful killeth him; for his hands refuse to labor.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.21.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He coveteth greedily all the day long: but the righteous giveth and spareth not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.21.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The sacrifice of the wicked ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " abomination: how much more, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "when",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he bringeth it with a wicked mind?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.21.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A false witness shall perish: but the man that heareth speaketh constantly.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.21.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A wicked man hardeneth his face: but ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the upright, he directeth his way.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.21.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no wisdom nor understanding nor counsel against the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.21.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The horse ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " prepared against the day of battle: but safety ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " from the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
